From 8ed086c17456207f712d65ce3df254faf42257a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:33:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] r4-prep 2/3: island sky dome + cloud layer follow the
 lakeside journey blend instead of covering the blended sky
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

During the island→lakeside blend the island env_sky_dome (builtin-unlit, opaque) covered the blended clear colour. The two existing
backdrop instances now take mainColor = lerp(island base (day 1 / night tint), lakesideEndClear / meanVertexColour, w) (SkyFollowCore,
linear): w=0 is exactly the island look, w=1 puts the dome average on the lakeside end clear (day 28/143/184, night 28/39/64); a
day/night toggle re-bases (follow keeps the blend, lakeside listener re-targets). Driven by LakesideJourneyLighting via
__worldDayNight.skyFollow(target,w) (identical frames skipped); restore sends exactly one null (island look back, before reapply).
No node, renderer, pass or material added (0 extra DC); WorldFlow dispose still releases the instances. Test lakeside-sky-follow.
